# Native tools — HARD (shell-interceptor)

**Do not** use Shell for file read, search, glob, in-place edit, file create/overwrite, or long-running services. Use the native tool. Hooks **deny** shadowed Shell with `permission: "deny"` — that is enforcement, not a suggestion.

| Instead of Shell | Required tool |
| ---------------- | ------------- |
| `cat` / `head` / `tail` | `Read` / `ReadFile` |
| `grep` / `rg` | `Grep` / `rg` |
| `find` / `fd` (name/type) | `Glob` |
| `sed -i` / `perl -i` | `StrReplace` / `ApplyPatch` |
| file redirects (`echo >`, etc.) | `Write` / `ApplyPatch` |
| `nohup`, `&`, `dev`/`watch` | `Task` / `Subagent` |

If a Shell call is denied, follow the redirect aliases. Do not retry the same shell pattern.

Shell is allowed for computing facts and real CLIs: `wc`, `diff`, `git`, build/test, `echo x > /dev/null`.
